> Run a command over every position in a shaped region, spread across ticks.

name Generation
slug bookshelf-generation
version 5.0.0
tags runtime
authors Aksiome

$run: #[command(slash="forbidden",empty="forbidden")] string

$cuboid:
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run at each position
    size: [int] @ 3 > number of positions on each axis, in the order of the function name: a negative number goes west, down or north
    batch?: int @ 1.. > positions done each tick, 256 by default
    on_finished?: $run > command to run once every position is done
  output state > the command runs at each position, over several ticks when there are more than `batch`

$rectangle:
  input arguments
    run: $run > command to run at each position
    size: [int] @ 2 > number of positions on each axis, in the order of the function name: a negative number goes west, down or north
    batch?: int @ 1.. > positions done each tick, 256 by default
    on_finished?: $run > command to run once every position is done
  output state > the command runs at each position, over several ticks when there are more than `batch`

$order3[xyz]:
  then: x, then y, then z
  and: x, y and z
  last: z
$order3[xzy]:
  then: x, then z, then y
  and: x, z and y
  last: y
$order3[yxz]:
  then: y, then x, then z
  and: y, x and z
  last: z
$order3[yzx]:
  then: y, then z, then x
  and: y, z and x
  last: x
$order3[zxy]:
  then: z, then x, then y
  and: z, x and y
  last: y
$order3[zyx]:
  then: z, then y, then x
  and: z, y and x
  last: x

$order2[xy]:
  then: x, then y
  and: x and y
$order2[xz]:
  then: x, then z
  and: x and z
$order2[yx]:
  then: y, then x
  and: y and x
$order2[yz]:
  then: y, then z
  and: y and z
$order2[zx]:
  then: z, then x
  and: z and x
$order2[zy]:
  then: z, then y
  and: z and y


feature function on_cuboid/$order3 > Run a command at each position of a cuboid, along $order3.then.
  since 2026/02/15 26.1
  @position > corner the cuboid starts from
  @dimension > dimension of the cuboid
  $cuboid

feature function on_cuboid_outline/$order3 > Run a command at each position on the outside of a cuboid sized along $order3.and, one layer along $order3.last at a time.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner the cuboid starts from
  @dimension > dimension of the cuboid
  $cuboid

feature function on_ellipse/$order2 > Run a command at each position inside an ellipse, the size being the one of the rectangle it fits in, along $order2.then.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner of the rectangle the ellipse fits in
  @dimension > dimension of the ellipse
  $rectangle

feature function on_ellipse_outline/$order2 > Run a command at each position on the edge of an ellipse, the size being the one of the rectangle it fits in, along $order2.then.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner of the rectangle the ellipse fits in
  @dimension > dimension of the ellipse
  $rectangle

feature function on_ellipsoid/$order3 > Run a command at each position inside an ellipsoid, the size being the one of the cuboid it fits in, along $order3.then.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner of the cuboid the ellipsoid fits in
  @dimension > dimension of the ellipsoid
  $cuboid

feature function on_ellipsoid_outline/$order3 > Run a command at each position on the outside of an ellipsoid, the size being the one of the cuboid it fits in, along $order3.then.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner of the cuboid the ellipsoid fits in
  @dimension > dimension of the ellipsoid
  $cuboid

feature function on_rectangle/$order2 > Run a command at each position of a rectangle, along $order2.then.
  since 2026/02/15 26.1
  @position > corner the rectangle starts from
  @dimension > dimension of the rectangle
  $rectangle

feature function on_rectangle_outline/$order2 > Run a command at each position on the edge of a rectangle sized along $order2.and, in no set order.
  since 2026/10/11 26.3
  @position > corner the rectangle starts from
  @dimension > dimension of the rectangle
  $rectangle

feature context_int_provider i > Get the index of the position a command runs at, on the first axis of the order.
  since 2026/10/09 26.3
  output result: int @ 0.. > index on the first axis, from 0

feature context_int_provider j > Get the index of the position a command runs at, on the second axis of the order.
  since 2026/10/09 26.3
  output result: int @ 0.. > index on the second axis, from 0

feature context_int_provider k > Get the index of the position a command runs at, on the third axis of the order, in a cuboid.
  since 2026/10/09 26.3
  output result: int @ 0.. > index on the third axis, from 0
